  "totalCostUsd": 0.023902700000000002,
  "result": "```python\ndef merge_intervals(intervals):\n    if not intervals:\n        return []\n    intervals = sorted(intervals, key=lambda iv: iv[0])\n    merged = [intervals[0]]\n    for start, end in intervals[1:]:\n        last_start, last_end = merged[-1]\n        if start <= last_end:\n            merged[-1] = (last_start, max(last_end, end))\n        else:\n            merged.append((start, end))\n    return merged\n```\n\nExample: `[(1,3),(2,6),(8,10)]` → `[(1,6),(8,10)]`.\n\n**Time: O(n log n)**. Sort dominates. Merge pass is O(n).\n**Space: O(n)** for output, plus sort overhead.\n\nTouching intervals like `(1,2),(2,3)` merge because of `<=`. Use `<` to keep them separate.",
